---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

export const prerender = true;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About · America's School Trust Library"
  description="A working library for the school trust lands — the 77 million acres set aside, beginning in 1785, to fund public education in perpetuity."
  sourceId="about-page"
>
  <article class="prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-a:text-blue-700 prose-a:underline">
    {/* v9 D.2 — small header mark for the Library seal. Library Mode
        only; image lands later (Cowork-side). onerror handler keeps
        the placeholder invisible until the asset is dropped in. */}
    <p class="library-seal-header-wrap">
      <button
        type="button"
        class="library-seal-button"
        data-seal-trigger
        aria-label="View library seal larger"
      >
        <img
          src="/seal/library-seal-v1.png"
          alt="America's School Trust Library seal"
          class="library-seal library-seal--header"
          onerror="this.style.display='none'"
        />
      </button>
    </p>

    <p class="kicker">About</p>
    <h1>About America's School Trust Library</h1>

    <p>
      America's School Trust Library is a working library for the school trust lands — the 77 million acres set aside, beginning in 1785, to fund public education in perpetuity.
    </p>

    <h2>Corporate record</h2>

    <p>
      America's School Trust Library is an Oregon nonprofit public benefit
      corporation. Its Articles of Incorporation were e-filed on July 21, 2026
      &mdash; Oregon Registry No. 259005891. The federal
      tax-exemption application has been filed; no determination has been issued.
    </p>

    <p>
      A volunteer board of directors governs the Library &mdash; no owners, no
      shareholders, no voting members. Governing documents:
      <a href="/governance/">Governance</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>The board</h2>

    <div class="board">
      <figure class="director">
        <img src="/board/sullivan.jpg" alt="Dave Sullivan" width="520" height="650" />
        <div>
        <span class="nm">Dave Sullivan</span>
        <span class="role">President &amp; Treasurer</span>
        <p>Founded the Library in 2026, after the record of one state's school-land promise turned out to be scattered &mdash; and every other state's scattered just as badly. Twenty-five years teaching information systems at Oregon State University's College of Business, where he holds an emeritus appointment; before that, a finance manager at Tektronix. He is also president of Oregon Advocates for School Trust Lands &mdash; a separate advocacy organization, and a dual role he discloses and sits out of whenever the two have business with each other.</p>
        </div>
      </figure>

      <figure class="director">
        <img src="/board/magee.jpg" alt="Kenneth &ldquo;Mike&rdquo; Magee" width="520" height="650" />
        <div>
        <span class="nm">Kenneth &ldquo;Mike&rdquo; Magee</span>
        <span class="role">Secretary</span>
        <p>Founded four Oregon companies across fifty years &mdash; accounting software for CPA firms in 1978; three personal-computer stores through the 1980s; Evergreen Technologies, a microprocessor-upgrade manufacturer he ran from a garage start to a subsidiary in England; and Belle Vallee Cellars, a Corvallis winery, until 2012. Mathematics and computer science at Western Washington State University, 1975. He coached academic and local startups as an executive in residence at the Oregon State University Accelerator until 2018. He and Dave Sullivan cofounded the Corvallis PC Club in the 1980s and have been friends since.</p>
        </div>
      </figure>

      <figure class="director">
        <img src="/board/shane.jpg" alt="Barry Shane" width="520" height="650" />
        <div>
        <span class="nm">Barry Shane</span>
        <span class="role">Director</span>
        <p>A professor of competitive strategy at Oregon State University. He has also taught strategy in graduate programs at universities in Taiwan, Thailand, and the Philippines.</p>
        </div>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <p>
      Portraits and records of the people who founded and advise the Library:
      the <a href="/founders/">Founders' Cabinet</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Who the Library works with</h2>

    <p>
      On August 10, 2026 the board of Oregon Advocates for School Trust Lands
      voted 3&ndash;0 to establish a non-exclusive alliance with the Library
      &mdash; limited to information, education, and preservation, and carrying
      no control, no agency, no financial obligation, and no litigation
      position on either side. Either board may end it at any time. OASTL is
      the advocacy organization Dave Sullivan also serves as president; he
      disclosed the dual role and sat out the vote. The Library's own board has
      not yet acted on it; the <a href="/organizing/">organizational record</a>
      will carry that action when it happens.
    </p>

    <p>
      What the alliance means in practice is that the Library expects to hold
      Oregon's school-trust record &mdash; including the Elliott State Forest
      material &mdash; on exactly the terms it holds anything else: catalogued
      without regard to whose argument it helps, free to every reader,
      corrected in public, and open to a reader who disagrees with every word
      OASTL has ever written. Keeping a document is not endorsing it. The
      Library takes no position in any case or campaign, and its
      <a href="/rights/">Constitution</a> forbids control by any advocacy
      organization &mdash; including that one. An alliance that could change
      what the shelves say would not be worth having, to either side.
    </p>

    <p>
      More on the founder's dual role: <a href="/independence/">Independence</a>.
    </p>

    <p>
      The Library's day-to-day building &mdash; cataloging, drafting, design,
      the back-end &mdash; is carried out in partnership with Claude, an AI
      system, under the direction of the Library's named human editors. No
      machine exercises final editorial authority, and no machine holds a
      corporate office or a seat on the board; the artificial-intelligence
      Librarian at the <a href="/reference-desk/">Reference Desk</a> answers
      readers from what the Library has already published.
      How that partnership works is described in
      <a href="/about/how-this-works/">How the Library Works</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>The rooms</h2>

    <ul>
      <li><a href="/catalog/">Catalog</a> &mdash; the index of the collection.</li>
      <li><a href="/reading/">Reading Room</a> &mdash; three book-length works.</li>
      <li><a href="/court/">Court Room</a> &mdash; rulings, filings, and case files.</li>
      <li><a href="/atlas/">Atlas</a> &mdash; fifty states under four lenses.</li>
      <li><a href="/maps/">Map Room</a> &mdash; where the trust lands are today.</li>
      <li><a href="/counting/">Counting House</a> &mdash; the financial record.</li>
      <li><a href="/newsroom/">Newsroom</a> &mdash; a weekly survey of what's changing.</li>
      <li><a href="/voices/">Voices</a> &mdash; signed editorial pieces.</li>
    </ul>

    <p class="becoming-pointer">
      How this Library is made: the <a href="/librarians/">Librarians' Room</a>.
      Or <button type="button" data-open-walking-tour class="walking-tour-link">take the walking tour</button>.
    </p>

    <style>
      .walking-tour-link {
        background: none;
        border: none;
        padding: 0;
        font: inherit;
        color: #1d4ed8;
        text-decoration: underline;
        cursor: pointer;
      }
    </style>

    <h2>Contact and corrections</h2>

    <p>
      Use the <strong>Submit Feedback</strong> and
      <strong>Submit Correction</strong> controls on any page. Every
      correction is dated and numbered in the
      <a href="/about/corrections/">corrections log</a>.
    </p>

    <p>
      See also: <a href="/about/cite/">How to Cite</a> &middot;
      <a href="/permissions/">Rights, Use, and Takedown</a> &middot;
      <a href="/about/founder/">The Founder's Statement</a>.
    </p>

    <hr class="archival-divider">

    <section class="signature-block">
      <p class="signature-dave">
        <span class="name">Dave Sullivan</span><br>
        <span class="role">President, America's School Trust Library</span>
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>

  <style>
    .kicker {
      font-family: var(--font-sans);
      font-size: 0.72rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.1em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: #A88A4E;
      margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
    }
    .becoming-pointer {
      margin: 1.4rem 0;
      padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
      background: #fafaf7;
      border-left: 3px solid #A88A4E;
      font-family: var(--font-serif);
      line-height: 1.55;
    }
    .featured-founder-card {
      margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;
      padding: 1.15rem 1.35rem;
      background: var(--linen-card, #fffdf7);
      border: 1px solid var(--rule-border, #d8d1c2);
      border-left: 3px solid var(--old-gold, #b88a2e);
      border-radius: 4px;
    }
    .featured-founder-card h2 {
      margin: 0 0 0.45rem;
      font-family: var(--font-serif);
      font-size: 1.2rem;
      line-height: 1.3;
      color: var(--deep-navy, #1f2a44);
    }
    .featured-founder-card p {
      margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
      font-family: var(--font-serif);
      line-height: 1.6;
    }
    .featured-founder-card__cta {
      margin: 0.4rem 0 0;
      font-family: var(--font-sans);
      font-size: 0.95rem;
    }

    /* The board. The site's reading measure is deliberately narrow, so the
       roster runs as rows — portrait beside the account — rather than fighting
       the column with three across. Grayscale is the house treatment: the
       portraits arrive in a mix of colour and black-and-white, and a uniform
       rendering reads as deliberate rather than accidental. */
    .board { margin: 0 0 1.6rem; }
    .board .director {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 124px 1fr;
      gap: 1.1rem;
      align-items: start;
      margin: 0 0 1.7rem;
    }
    .board .director img,
    .board .director .ph {
      width: 124px;
      aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
      object-fit: cover;
      display: block;
      border-radius: 3px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(31, 42, 68, 0.25);
      box-shadow: 0 1px 4px rgba(14, 32, 56, 0.18);
      margin: 0;
    }
    .board .director .ph {
      border: 1px dashed #C9A24A;
      box-shadow: none;
      background: #EDE3CC;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      text-align: center;
      font-family: var(--font-sans);
      font-size: 0.6rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.12em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: #8a6d1f;
      padding: 0 0.5rem;
    }
    .board .director .nm {
      display: block;
      font-family: var(--font-serif);
      color: var(--deep-navy, #1f2a44);
      font-size: 1.08rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      line-height: 1.25;
      margin: 0 0 0.1rem;
    }
    .board .director .role {
      display: block;
      font-family: var(--font-sans);
      font-size: 0.7rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.11em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: #8a6d1f;
      margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    }
    .board .director p {
      font-family: var(--font-serif);
      font-size: 0.92rem;
      line-height: 1.6;
      margin: 0;
    }
    .board .director p.tocome { font-style: italic; color: #5b6b82; }
    @media (max-width: 420px) {
      .board .director { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.6rem; }
      .board .director img,
      .board .director .ph { width: 150px; }
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
